## Evidence Base

### OOS Validation Results (train pre-2025 → test 2025+)

| Strategy | Config | TRAIN DD | TEST DD | TEST Sharpe | OOS Valid |
|----------|--------|----------|---------|-------------|----------|
| S56 | ADV 75M + GRAD 15/25/40 168h | -15.58% | -10.06% | 6.230 | YES |
| S60 | ADV 100M + GRAD 25/40/60 168h | -14.87% | -9.43% | 6.855 | YES |
| S56 | ADV only (no pump) | -15.63% | -12.19% | 6.112 | — |
| S60 | ADV only (no pump) | -18.56% | -9.66% | 6.810 | — |

Previous 6mo-only recommendation (GRAD 20/30/40 168h for S60) FAILED OOS validation.
Wider thresholds survive because they only block extreme pumps.

### Backtesting Audit Findings

| # | Issue | Severity | Est. Metric Inflation |
|---|-------|----------|----------------------|
| 1 | MaxDD on daily resampled equity (not hourly) | CRITICAL | DD understated 1.7-2.4x |
| 2 | Unrestricted compounding ($200K → $391M) | CRITICAL | Late returns are fantasy |
| 3 | Walk-forward training period in equity curve | HIGH | Annualized return diluted |
| 4 | Slippage uses daily ADV, fills within 1 hour | HIGH | Slippage understated ~5x at scale |
| 5 | Sharpe uses daily closes not hourly | MEDIUM | 10-30% Sharpe inflation |

Calmar reported 80-400 → corrected estimate 8-15. Still excellent, but ~8x inflated.

## Implementation Plan

### Phase 1: Metrics Fix (P0 — do first, affects all subsequent analysis)

#### 1A: Hourly MaxDD in metrics pipeline
- File: `v4/metrics.py` — `compute_metrics()`
- Change: Accept optional hourly equity series; compute MaxDD on hourly if provided
- File: `v4/report.py` — `compute_portfolio_metrics()`
- Change: Pass hourly equity to metrics, not daily resampled
- Calmar = annualized_return / abs(hourly_max_dd)
- Sharpe/Sortino remain on daily (convention), but note hourly DD in output
- Add `max_dd_hourly_pct` field to PerformanceMetrics

#### 1B: Exclude walk-forward training period from annualization
- File: `v4/metrics.py` — `compute_metrics()`
- Find first non-flat equity bar (first trade) and compute `years` from there
- Or accept `trading_start_idx` parameter

#### 1C: Capacity-aware return reporting
- Add `capacity_equity_cap` to PortfolioConfig (default None = uncapped)
- When set, stop compounding above the cap (excess equity stays as cash)
- Realistic default: $5M for perp strategies
- This doesn't change the simulation, just caps position sizing growth

### Phase 2: ADV-Scaled Position Sizing (P0 — structural, mandatory)

#### 2A: Add ADV sizing to StrategySpec
- File: `v4/config.py`
- New fields on StrategySpec:
  - `adv_sizing_enabled: bool = False`
  - `adv_sizing_base: float = 100_000_000`  # $100M default
  - `adv_sizing_floor: float = 0.20`  # 20% minimum
- Formula: `size_mult = min(1.0, max(floor, sqrt(adv_24h / base)))`

#### 2B: Apply in simulator entry path
- File: `v4/simulator.py` — `_process_entries()`
- After position is created, apply ADV sizing multiplier
- Uses 24h rolling ADV from the token's volume data
- Multiplier applied to: margin_usd, quantity, initial_risk

#### 2C: Strategy-specific parameters
- S56 (+ s69, s76 which inherit): base=$75M, floor=0.20
- S60: base=$100M, floor=0.20
- Other strategies: evaluate individually, default OFF

### Phase 3: Graduated Pump Filter (P1 — OOS-validated)

#### 3A: Add graduated pump fields to StrategySpec
- File: `v4/config.py`
- New fields:
  - `pump_grad_enabled: bool = False`
  - `pump_grad_window: int = 168`  # hours lookback
  - `pump_grad_t1: float = 0.15`   # >t1 → 50% size
  - `pump_grad_t2: float = 0.25`   # >t2 → 25% size
  - `pump_grad_t3: float = 0.40`   # >t3 → full block
  - `pump_grad_longs_only: bool = True`

#### 3B: Apply in simulator entry path
- File: `v4/simulator.py` — `_process_entries()`
- After ADV sizing (Phase 2), apply graduated pump filter
- Compute: `ret = (close[bar] - close[bar - window]) / close[bar - window]`
- Apply graduated sizing or block based on thresholds
- Only on LONG direction if longs_only=True

#### 3C: Strategy-specific parameters (OOS-validated)
- S56: window=168, t1=0.15, t2=0.25, t3=0.40
- S60: window=168, t1=0.25, t2=0.40, t3=0.60
- Other strategies: evaluate individually, default OFF

### Phase 4: Slippage Model Fix (P2 — improves realism)

#### 4A: Use hourly volume for participation rate
- File: `v4/sizing.py`
- Change participation calc from `position_size / daily_adv` to `position_size / (daily_adv / 24)`
- This makes slippage 24x more realistic for hourly fills
- Will increase fee drag, especially on large positions

### Phase 5: Verification & Paper Deploy (P3)

#### 5A: Re-run backtest with ALL fixes applied
- Compare old metrics vs corrected metrics
- Verify Calmar is now in realistic range (8-20, not 80-400)
- Verify hourly MaxDD matches what filter sweep scripts computed

#### 5B: Update paper trader config
- Add ADV sizing + graduated pump filter to strategy configs
- Restart paper trader with new parameters
- Monitor for 50+ trades before declaring success

#### 5C: Document results
- Update PROJECT_STATUS.md with corrected metrics
- Record findings in strategy-findings.jsonl
- Close .strategy-mission-anti-crash-filters (superseded)

## Safety Constraints

- Paper trader PID running 21 pools — ALL testing in isolation
- Do NOT modify live v4/simulator.py until Phase 1 metrics fix is verified
- Phase 2-3 filters: implement in production code but behind StrategySpec flags (default OFF)
- Phase 5: flip flags ON only after re-verification

## Kill Criteria

- If OOS-validated filters degrade 24mo Sharpe by >0.5 when applied to production code → re-evaluate
- If corrected Calmar < 3.0 for either strategy → fundamental strategy quality issue
- If hourly slippage fix causes >50% return degradation → slippage model may be over-penalizing

